# Default owner for everything not matched by a more specific rule.
#
# Two owners, deliberately. GitHub will not let an author approve their own
# pull request, so a sole owner who is also the only person opening pull
# requests makes `require_code_owner_review` impossible to satisfy rather than
# strict: every pull request stays blocked with nothing left to do. The second
# owner is what makes the rule enforceable instead of deadlocked.
#
# Multiple owners for one pattern must share a single line; consecutive lines
# do not stack, the last matching line wins.
